\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Reporting-layer sensitivity of the second-bed MATH500 composite gap to judge convention and anchor-count uncertainty. Takeaway: the citable verdict is \emph  {judge-convention-dependent}. Under the lenient judge with the $30$-anchor pair-bias correction (row~1) the read is \textsc  {power\_limited} ($+0.1606\ [-0.059,+0.380]$). Under the validated v2 judge, the measured anchor pair-bias is $0$ (v2 agrees with all $30$ human anchors; $0$ discordant), so the v2 read (row~3) is positive and excludes $0$ ($+0.2382\ [0.1639,0.3125]$). We report both honestly rather than fixing a single convention; rows~3--5 keep the v2 point and vary the anchor-\emph  {uncertainty} index $k\in \{0,1,2\}$; the $\sqrt  {k}/10$ propagation is a conservative convenience bound on the purposive anchor, \emph  {not} an identified sampling standard error, with $\mathrm  {se_{bias}}(k)=\sqrt  {k}/10$ where $k$ is the count of discordant anchors over a $10$-per-tier $t_0\cup t_2$ gradient subset (row~1 is implicitly $k{=}1$). Panel (b) makes the denominator-sensitive audit explicit.}}{11}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:convention}{{6}{11}{Reporting-layer sensitivity of the second-bed MATH500 composite gap to judge convention and anchor-count uncertainty. Takeaway: the citable verdict is \emph {judge-convention-dependent}. Under the lenient judge with the $30$-anchor pair-bias correction (row~1) the read is \textsc {power\_limited} ($+0.1606\ [-0.059,+0.380]$). Under the validated v2 judge, the measured anchor pair-bias is $0$ (v2 agrees with all $30$ human anchors; $0$ discordant), so the v2 read (row~3) is positive and excludes $0$ ($+0.2382\ [0.1639,0.3125]$). We report both honestly rather than fixing a single convention; rows~3--5 keep the v2 point and vary the anchor-\emph {uncertainty} index $k\in \{0,1,2\}$; the $\sqrt {k}/10$ propagation is a conservative convenience bound on the purposive anchor, \emph {not} an identified sampling standard error, with $\mathrm {se_{bias}}(k)=\sqrt {k}/10$ where $k$ is the count of discordant anchors over a $10$-per-tier $t_0\cup t_2$ gradient subset (row~1 is implicitly $k{=}1$). Panel (b) makes the denominator-sensitive audit explicit}{table.6}{}}
